  notes:"The overproof bourbon is non-negotiable — it provides the backbone that makes this drink work. Without it, the amaretto overwhelms. Morgenthaler's documented preference is Bookers (typically 120–130 proof, uncut and unfiltered straight from the barrel) as first choice, with Old Grand-Dad 114 as the excellent more accessible option. Any cask-strength bourbon in the 110–130 proof range works. For amaretto, he calls for Lazzaroni — lighter and more almond-forward than the more common DiSaronno. Dry shake first, then shake with ice. Fine strain.",
