  instructions:"Add the quartered lime to a shaker tin and muddle firmly to release the juice. Add tequila, Demerara syrup, ginger syrup, Tabasco, and rose water. Fill with ice and shake hard. Dump the entire contents unstrained into a chilled double rocks glass. Top with additional ice if needed. No garnish. For Demerara syrup: 1 cup Demerara sugar, half cup water, simmer until dissolved, cool and bottle. Refrigerates up to 2 weeks. For fresh ginger syrup: juice three quarters lb peeled ginger root, add sugar at a ratio of one third cup sugar per half cup juice, blend on high for 2 minutes until fully dissolved. Refrigerates up to 1 week.",
