  lore:"Created by Matt Piacentini at The Up and Up in Greenwich Village, New York in 2016 — the year every guest seemed to ask the same question: do you have any spicy tequila drinks? The name comes from the scene in It is a Wonderful Life where George Bailey, returned from his supernatural journey, finds his daughter Zuzu's flower petals in his coat pocket. The petals are proof that Bedford Falls is restored and that he was never erased from it. In the cocktail, as in the film, just a few drops of rose water — petals in liquid form — transform a rustic blend of tequila, lime, ginger, and Demerara into something aromatic and ethereal. Piacentini has watched the film every year at Christmas since film school in London, and describes it as a full recharge of the gratitude meter. The cocktail became the most popular drink at The Up and Up by a significant margin. It is a celebration of the vibrance of simply being alive.",
