  instructions:"For the vanilla honey syrup: dissolve honey in an equal volume of warm water and add a drop of vanilla extract. Combine all ingredients in a shaker with crushed or pebble ice and 3-4 ice cubes. Shake until well chilled and frosty. Pour unstrained into a tiki mug or tall glass — the ice goes in with the drink. Garnish with a pineapple leaf, three cocktail cherries on a pick, and a pineapple spear or wedge. The orchid is optional but encouraged.",
  notes:"Use a dry curacao rather than a sweet triple sec — the distinction matters here. Rhum agricole and Jamaican rum together give the drink both the grassy brightness of cane juice rum and the funky depth of molasses rum. The unstrained pour is deliberate — the dilution and texture from the crushed ice is part of the drink. Three cherries on the garnish is not decoration; the name is Morse code for V, the victory symbol. This spec by Dushan Zaric omits the orange juice of the original Donn Beach recipe, which the modern craft tiki world has largely endorsed.",
  tastingNotes:"",
