  lore:"Created by Donn Beach — born Ernest Raymond Beaumont Gantt — at Don the Beachcomber in Hollywood in the 1940s. The name is Morse code for the letter V, the victory sign, and was created as a celebration of the Allied victory in World War II. Three dots and a dash — dot dot dot dash — the most famous letter in the history of radio transmission. The version in this collection was developed by Dushan Zaric, the cocktail architect behind Employees Only and Macao Trading Co in New York City, for the relaunch of one of Southern California oldest tiki bars. Zaric removed the orange juice of the original, tightening the spec and pushing the rum and spice elements forward. Donn Beach invented tiki. This drink is why.",
  source:"https://drunkardsalmanac.com/three-dots-and-a-dash-cocktail/",
