  instructions:"Add mint leaves and simple syrup to a julep cup or rocks glass. Press the mint gently with a muddler — bruise, do not shred. Add bourbon and fill with crushed ice, packing it tightly. Stir briefly to combine. Mound more crushed ice above the rim. Garnish with a generous bouquet of fresh mint pressed close to the straw so the nose is buried in it on every sip. Serve with a short straw.",
  notes:"The short straw is essential — it forces the nose into the mint bouquet. Crushed ice is non-negotiable; cubed ice produces a different, inferior drink. Press the mint, do not pulverize it. A Julep cup chills beautifully and frosts on the outside, which is part of the ritual. Wheated bourbons work particularly well here.",
