  instructions:"Prepare the glass first: moisten the rim of a coupe with a lemon wedge and dip in fine sugar to create the crusta. Peel a long spiral of lemon peel and place it inside the glass so it lines the interior — this is the defining presentation. Combine cognac, Cointreau, lemon juice, maraschino, and bitters in a shaker with ice. Shake until well chilled. Strain carefully into the prepared glass.",
  notes:"The long spiral lemon peel lining the glass interior is not optional — it is the crusta that names the drink. The presentation is the point. Take time with it. Fine sugar gives a more elegant crust than coarse. The drink is quite dry; the sugar rim and maraschino provide the only sweetness.",
