  lore:"Created by Joseph Santini at the City Exchange bar in New Orleans around 1850 — making it one of the oldest identifiable cocktail recipes in American history. The Brandy Crusta is the missing link between the Fancy Cocktail of the 1840s and the Sidecar of the 1920s. It introduced the sugar-rimmed glass and the citrus peel lining — both of which became defining elements of classic cocktail presentation. Without the Brandy Crusta there is no Sidecar, and without the Sidecar there is arguably no Daisy family. Jerry Thomas included it in his 1862 How to Mix Drinks, cementing its place in the canon. It fell out of fashion for over a century before the craft cocktail revival restored it to its proper place: at the beginning of everything.",
