  instructions:"Add all ingredients to a blender and blend until smooth. Serve in a rocks glass. Garnish with a brulee sugar crisp. For the Old Fashioned mix: combine 150ml black tea, 150g sugar, and 14 dashes aromatic bitters. Stir until sugar dissolves. For the citrus blend: combine 2 parts fresh lemon juice, 1 part fresh orange juice, 1 part fresh grapefruit juice. For the brulee sugar crisp: cut the end off an orange and place it upside down on a jigger. Spread 1 barspoon sugar over the center, add 8-10 drops aromatic bitters, then caramelize with a kitchen torch until fully browned and bubbling. Add a pinch of flaky sea salt as it cools.",
  notes:"Xanthan gum is optional but recommended for texture — it prevents the blend from separating and gives the drink a smoother, more uniform consistency. A small amount goes a long way. Pre-made old fashioned mix and sour mix can substitute for the house-made versions but the scratch version is dramatically better. The brulee sugar crisp can be made ahead and stored briefly.",
