  notes:"Equal parts is the classic spec. Craddock's original called for Kina Lillet, which no longer exists — Lillet Blanc is the modern standard but Cocchi Americano gives a more bitter, quinine-forward result closer to the original. Cointreau specifically for the orange liqueur. The absinthe is a rinse only — swirl and discard the excess.",
