  lore:"Harry Craddock, head bartender at the American Bar at the Savoy Hotel in London, published this in The Savoy Cocktail Book in 1930 alongside the only instruction anyone remembers: Four of these taken in swift succession will unrevive the corpse again. The drink belongs to a family of cocktails called Corpse Revivers, originally intended as hair-of-the-dog hangover remedies — a tradition documented as far back as 1861 in Punch magazine. The No. 2 overtook every other version in the canon and never looked back. It is one of the great equal-parts cocktails: gin, Cointreau, Lillet, lemon, each pulling equal weight, with the absinthe rinse adding a fifth voice from the glass itself.",
