  notes:"Three ingredients. The quality of each matters enormously. A good London Dry with botanical complexity is the right choice — the orgeat needs a gin with something to say. Liber & Co. orgeat is the house recommendation. The original 2:1:1 recipe (equal parts gin, lemon, orgeat) is too sweet; the 8:2:1 Embury version is too dry. The balanced 8:3:2 ratio — 2oz gin, 3/4oz lemon, 1/2oz orgeat — is where this drink lives.",
  tastingNotes:"",
