  lore:"One of the great deep cuts of the classic cocktail canon, and one of the most underserved. First appears — as a name only, with no recipe — in William Tarling 1937 Cafe Royal Bar Book. The first actual recipe arrives in David Embury 1948 The Fine Art of Mixing Drinks, where Embury published the original 2:1:1 formula alongside his own withering assessment: I have given you the original recipe, which I think is horrible. Embury thinned it out considerably; subsequent bartenders found the middle ground. The drink may have originated at The Army and Navy Club in Washington D.C., the same officers club said to have introduced the Daiquiri to the United States. Nobody knows for certain, which is partly why it remains a deep cut rather than a household name. It deserves better.",
  source:"https://punchdrink.com/articles/army-navy-gin-sour-cocktail/",
