  instructions:"Add tequila, lime juice, and ginger syrup to a shaker with a few ice cubes and whip-shake briefly — just enough to combine and chill without over-diluting. Strain into a Collins glass. Top with club soda and add ice. Float the sweet vermouth over the back of a bar spoon so it sits on top. Garnish with a mint sprig.",
  notes:"The whip shake is a specific technique worth understanding: use just 2-3 ice cubes instead of a full shaker of ice, and shake briefly — 3 to 5 seconds rather than the usual 12-15. The goal is to combine and slightly chill the ingredients without the full dilution of a standard shake. When you then add soda, you preserve the carbonation and get a fresher, livelier drink than if you had fully shaken and diluted first. It is the right technique for any drink that gets topped with a sparkling element. The sweet vermouth float is the signature move: it perfumes every sip from the nose and adds a layer of complexity that arrives at the end of each sip. Fell to Earth is a Philadelphia producer making exceptional vermouth; any quality sweet vermouth works. Teremana blanco is the house recommendation.",
