  instructions:"Combine all ingredients in a rocks glass without ice and stir to combine. Add one large ice cube and stir again until well chilled. Express a flamed orange twist over the drink — hold a match to the skin side of the peel for a few seconds, then squeeze the oils toward the flame so they ignite briefly. Drop the singed peel into the drink.",
  notes:"The reposado tequila replicates the oaky, aged character of whiskey while the mezcal adds smoke and depth. Ward's original spec: El Tesoro Reposado tequila and Del Maguey San Luis del Rio mezcal — the latter being a small-batch single-village mezcal with significant complexity. Agave nectar in place of simple syrup ties the sweetener to the spirit. Many bartenders now use a 2:1 tequila-to-mezcal split; the original was equal parts. Both work.",
