  tastingNotes:"",
  lore:"Created by Phil Ward at Death and Co in New York City in 2007, the Oaxacan Old Fashioned is the most requested and most imitated cocktail Death and Co has ever produced — and the drink credited with opening the American cocktail world to the possibilities of mezcal. Ward replaced whiskey with a split base of reposado tequila and mezcal, and simple syrup with agave nectar. The result was something that felt entirely familiar in structure and entirely new in character. Cocktail writer Robert Simonson wrote that it opened mixologists eyes to the potential of tequila and mezcal in ways that had not been seen before. Ward went on to co-found Mayahuel, New York first dedicated mezcal and tequila bar. The Oaxacan Old Fashioned is what a truly great riff looks like — same template, transformed spirit.",
