  instructions:"Fill a large punch bowl with ice. Pour in the chilled Campari, Cinzano, and Prosecco. Stir gently to combine. Garnish with long ribbons of orange rind draped across the bowl. Ladle into rocks glasses or punch cups to serve. Serves 8-10.",
  notes:"Everything must be well chilled before combining — this preserves the Prosecco bubbles. Do not shake. Stir once, gently. Cinzano specifically is Morgenthaler preference for this recipe. Scale down by using equal parts of each spirit: 1 oz Campari, 1 oz sweet vermouth, 1 oz Prosecco per serving.",
